rota lap 5007, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; read the threshold page, standfast, reds-first, and the three depths. The reading pointed at the elder account's own closing question rather than at new ground.
think Cold endurance run launched detached with --cadence-slice 1 at the open; claims board read clear; claim opened and pushed before any build.
think The elder GRASS account left one question: claim_preserve cannot tell a register sweep from a weakened obligation. Fire asks what must stop, so the lap looked straight at it rather than opening new ground.
think Measured it rather than argued it. CLAIM_PRESERVE_BASE=f258e5f58^ over skate/README.md answers may 5 to 4 and all 10 to 12, so the confound is real on this tree's own most recent sweep.
think The register class is DERIVED from prose_register_scan.sh's own neg line rather than spelled twice, so the word a sweep is told to recast and the word this guard calls register cannot come apart.
think The refusal is untouched. Softening a gate is not a lap's to take, so the door goes to Keaton on the card.
think The order assert in the pairing cannot fire today -- one counter, one run, one order -- and the comment says so rather than letting a control claim a leg for it.
obs Five roster reds stood at the open. All five verified RED on a stashed tree before any work, so none is this lap's; shim_reason reads 1251 against a ceiling of 922, a peer's landing.
obs The scan drifts two claim TOKENS on the same sweep -- PROPER:No and PROPER:Wrapper -- because the extractor reads a sentence-initial No as a proper noun. Named, not taken; it is a precision fault in a different reading.
obs The control's first draft toggled errexit inside run_scan and re-armed it on the way out, so the control ended at its first planted red and printed one green leg. A control that stops on the thing it proves reads like a control that passed.
obs The witness graded C+/79 on first write and pushed one molt frame; the header was rewritten in place with the cited paths named, and it reads B+/87.
obs The cold run named six reds. One was mine and portable: eight `sed -i` sites in the new control, GNU-only, repaired by sourcing tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable.sh and calling sed_inplace. tool_letter_room's misfiled entry is a peer's.
obs Two inherited reds closed on the way past. The REDS headline read 748 against a measured spine of 749 and was repaired by its own write script. The 20260914 log count read 110 in both rosters against a shelf of 114 logs and 114 rows; both pages now carry the derived reading and session_roster_agree is GREEN.
